  "summary": "Package sends host and environment data to hardcoded Telegram bot endpoint on install and at runtime",
  "details": "The package contains multiple code paths that collect host information (process.env, process.platform, hostname, whoami output, filesystem enumeration) and transmit it to hardcoded network destinations. setup.js and health.js issue HTTPS requests to api.telegram.org (a Telegram Bot API endpoint, which typically indicates a hardcoded bot token used as a C2/notification channel) alongside child_process usage and filesystem reads. bot.js reads the filesystem and posts collected data over https. core/scheduler.js spawns an 'sh' subprocess. The combination of hardcoded api.telegram.org calls with host reconnaissance (hostname, whoami, process.env, process.platform) and shell execution across setup.js, health.js, bot.js, and core/handlers.js matches the credential/host-exfiltration and remote-command shape rather than a documented product feature.",
